# Stage 10 — uppercase class names, constants and JS globals.
#
# 57 identifiers, the last GF-prefixed family in the tree. These are PHP and JS
# class names (GFConditionalLogic, GF_Theme_Layer, GF_JSON_Handler), service
# container constants (GF_FORMS, GF_COMMON, GF_API) and JS globals (GFMergeTag,
# GFCalc, GFPaymentObj). None of the eight add-ons references any of them.
#
# Six are merges rather than renames, because the target already exists — the
# same half-applied pattern seen throughout: GFAsyncUpload, GFFeedOrder,
# GFFrontendFeeds, GFPageConditionalLogic, GFToken and GF_Field_CAPTCHA all
# have a KDNA-prefixed twin already in the tree.
#
# Naming rule: where the f belongs to the following word — GFORMS, gform,
# gfield, ginput — only the g changes, giving KFORMS, kform, kfield, kinput.
# Where the GF is the Gravity Forms abbreviation and the next letters start a
# new word, the whole GF becomes KDNA. That is why GFORMS_DOING_MOCK goes to
# KFORMS_DOING_MOCK and not KDNAORMS_DOING_MOCK.
#
# GF_Forms_Model_Legacy is renamed but stays a class that does not exist here.
# It is the legacy model the schema version gates, and reaching it fatals the
# site either way; the rename neither helps nor hurts that, and the landmine is
# documented in CLAUDE.md.
#
# Five more are handled in a separate pass because their correct target is not
# the mechanical one and several would collide: GFcommon is a real fatal
# (KDNACommon), GForms and GFSystemStatus are docblocks that both point at
# KDNAForms, GFField_CAPTCHA is KDNA_Field_CAPTCHA, and GFFrontEndFeeds is a
# misspelling of GFFrontendFeeds.

GFConditionalLogic                           KDNAConditionalLogic
GF_Forms_Model_Legacy                        KDNA_Forms_Model_Legacy
GF_CONDITIONAL_INSTANCES_COLLECTION          KDNA_CONDITIONAL_INSTANCES_COLLECTION
